  <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#F5F5F5] sm:text-4xl">
    About Moview
  </h1>

  <div class="review-prose mt-8">
    <p>
      <strong>Moview</strong> ({{ site.domain }}) is an independent editorial publication dedicated to honest, readable reviews of Hindi and Bollywood cinema, direct-to-OTT films, and Indian web series.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every review published on Moview is written from scratch with a focus on craft, storytelling, pacing, and whether a title genuinely deserves your time on the weekend.
    </p>

    <h2>Our Rating Scale &amp; Verdicts</h2>
    <p>
      Each film or season is scored out of 10 and paired with one of four straightforward verdicts so you can decide in seconds:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Must Watch (8.5 – 10.0)</strong>: Essential viewing that excels in writing, direction, and performances.</li>
      <li><strong>Worth Watching (7.0 – 8.4)</strong>: Strong, engaging work that holds up despite minor flaws.</li>
      <li><strong>One-Time Watch (5.0 – 6.9)</strong>: Watchable entertainment for fans of the genre or cast, without lasting depth.</li>
      <li><strong>Skip It (0.0 – 4.9)</strong>: Misses the mark in execution and is easy to pass over.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Spoiler Policy</h2>
    <p>
      Most reviews avoid revealing third-act twists. Whenever a critique needs to discuss major plot developments or endings, a clear Spoiler Warning banner is placed at the very top of the review.
    </p>
  </div>
